---
import PluginDocsLayout from '../../layouts/PluginDocsLayout.astro';
import Diagram from '../../components/Diagram.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';

const manifest = `{
  "id": "hello",
  "name": "Hello",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "protocol_version": 1,
  "author": "you",
  "url": "https://example.com",
  "license": "MIT",
  "description": "How and when to use this plugin, advertised to the agent.",
  "main": "hello-plugin",
  "settings": { "greeting": "Hello" },
  "completion": {
    "hello": {
      "help": "one-line drawer description",
      "man": "Manual page: use case, usage, examples.",
      "children": {
        "greet": { "help": "Greet someone", "man": "Usage: /hello greet <name>" }
      }
    }
  },
  "tools": [
    { "name": "greet",
      "description": "Greet someone by name.",
      "schema": { "name": {"type": "string", "required": true} } }
  ]
}`;

const layout = `~/.config/amber/plugins/hello/
├── manifest.json      # id, name, version, protocol_version, main, tools[], completion{}
└── hello-plugin       # executable, chmod +x`;

const initialize = `// harness -> plugin
{"id": 1, "method": "initialize", "params": {
  "protocol_version": 1,
  "settings": { "greeting": "Hello" },
  "workspace": "/path/to/workspace"}}

// plugin -> harness
{"id": 1, "result": {"protocol_version": 1, "ok": true}}`;

const toolCall = `// harness -> plugin
{"id": 2, "method": "tool.call",
 "params": {"name": "greet", "args": {"name": "amber"}}}

// plugin -> harness  (the standard tool envelope)
{"id": 2, "result": {"ok": true, "output": "Hello, amber!", "meta": {}}}

// errors are returned, never thrown:
{"id": 2, "result": {"ok": false, "output": "ERROR: ..."}}`;

const shutdown = `{"method": "shutdown"}   // notification; the plugin exits cleanly`;

const protocolDir = `${site.repo}/blob/main/docs/spec/plugins/README.md`;
---

<PluginDocsLayout
  title="External plugins"
  description="The amber external plugin protocol: manifest.json, JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdio, lifecycle, administration and security."
  current="external"
>
  <h1>External plugins</h1>

  <p>
    External plugins are self-contained executables that extend amber with new
    tools. The harness never links plugin code: every plugin is a separate
    process speaking newline-delimited JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdio, so a plugin
    crash cannot take down the app and protocol changes ship as plugin updates
    without touching the core.
  </p>

  <p>
    They contribute <strong>tools only</strong>. For anything else, providers,
    status segments, panels, prompt blocks, event hooks, use a
    <a href="/plugins/anatomy">core plugin</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Layout and discovery</h2>
  <div class="terminal"><pre>{layout}</pre></div>
  <p>Search order (first hit wins):</p>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li><code>$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/amber/plugins/&lt;id&gt;</code></li>
    <li><code>~/.config/amber/plugins/&lt;id&gt;</code></li>
    <li><code>&lt;workspace&gt;/.amber/plugins/&lt;id&gt;</code></li>
    <li><code>$(datadir)/amber/plugins/&lt;id&gt;</code> (system-shipped)</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Manifest</h2>
  <div class="terminal"><pre>{manifest}</pre></div>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Required</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>id</code></td><td>yes</td><td>Slug <code>[a-z0-9_]+</code>; directory name, tool prefix, namespace root.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>name</code></td><td>yes</td><td>Display name.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>version</code></td><td>yes</td><td>Semver.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>protocol_version</code></td><td>yes</td><td>Integer. The harness rejects a mismatch (<em>incompatible</em>).</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>description</code></td><td>yes</td><td>Prompt advertisement: how/when to use the tools, rendered while enabled.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>main</code></td><td>yes</td><td>Executable path relative to the plugin directory.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>author</code> / <code>url</code> / <code>license</code></td><td>no</td><td>Attribution, shown by <code>/get plugin info &lt;id&gt;</code>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>settings</code></td><td>no</td><td>Default key/value settings; overridden via <code>/set plugin settings &lt;id&gt; &lt;key&gt;=&lt;value&gt;</code>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>completion</code></td><td>no</td><td>A completions.json subtree merged into the command tree on enable.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>tools</code></td><td>no</td><td>Tool definitions, registered as <code>plugin_&lt;id&gt;_&lt;name&gt;</code>.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Protocol</h2>
  <p>One JSON object per line on stdin/stdout, UTF-8. All messages carry an <code>id</code> except notifications.</p>
  <Diagram
    name="externalPluginHandshake"
  />

  <h3>initialize</h3>
  <div class="terminal"><pre>{initialize}</pre></div>
  <p>
    A <code>protocol_version</code> mismatch or <code>"ok": false</code> marks
    the plugin incompatible and unregisters it.
  </p>

  <h3>tool.call</h3>
  <div class="terminal"><pre>{toolCall}</pre></div>
  <p>
    The result is the same tool envelope the built-in tools use, so the agent
    reads a plugin result exactly like a <code>bash</code> or
    <code>search</code> result.
  </p>

  <h3>shutdown</h3>
  <div class="terminal"><pre>{shutdown}</pre></div>

  <h3>Timeouts</h3>
  <p>
    A tool call that produces no line within 60&nbsp;s is killed and reported as
    a timeout. Partial output is lost, plugins must emit one line per request.
  </p>

  <h2>Administration</h2>
  <div class="terminal"><pre>{`/get plugin list | info <id> | settings <id> [key]
/set plugin on <id> | off <id> | install <path|url> | uninstall <id>
/set plugin settings <id> <key>=<value>`}</pre></div>
  <p>
    <code>install</code> takes a tar.gz (local path or http(s) URL) containing
    <code>manifest.json</code> and the executable; it is validated and staged to
    <code>~/.config/amber/plugins/&lt;id&gt;/</code>, left disabled until
    <code>/set plugin on &lt;id&gt;</code>. System-shipped plugins
    cannot be uninstalled.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <ul class="feature-list">
    <li>Plugin code is <strong>untrusted</strong> but runs with the user's privileges, like the harness. Install only plugins you trust; <code>/get plugin info &lt;id&gt;</code> shows author/url/license before enabling.</li>
    <li>All path arguments pass through workspace confinement before the plugin sees them.</li>
    <li>Output is capped at 64&nbsp;KiB per tool result.</li>
    <li>Tools are namespaced <code>plugin_&lt;id&gt;_&lt;name&gt;</code>, so approval rules can target them by name.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Known limitation</h2>
  <p>
    Command subtrees contributed by external plugins render in the completion
    drawer but <strong>cannot execute</strong>: no handler is registered for
    <code>plugin.*</code> actions. The command-contribution capability was
    removed (nothing produced or consumed one). Expose behaviour through tools
    instead.
  </p>

  <p>
    Full protocol: <a href={protocolDir} rel="noopener">docs/spec/plugins/README.md</a>.
  </p>
</PluginDocsLayout>

<style>
  .steps {
    color: #9a7c47;
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.9;
    padding-left: 20px;
  }
</style>
